---
description: Depot Add License Header
globs: *
---
# Add License Header

Automatically add license headers to new files.

<rule>
name: add_license_header
description: Automatically add license headers to new files and update existing ones
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "*"
  - type: event
    pattern: "file_create"
  - type: intent
    pattern: "update.*license"

actions:
  - type: execute
    command: "depot-addlicense \"$FILE\""
    require_user_approval: false

  - type: suggest
    message: |
      License headers should follow these formats:

      Go files:
      ```go
      // Copyright (c) 2025 Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      // SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary
      ```

      Nix files:
      ```nix
      # Copyright (c) 2025 Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary
      ```

      Shell files:
      ```bash
      # Copyright (c) 2025 Geoffrey Huntley <ghuntley@ghuntley.com>. All rights reserved.
      # SPDX-License-Identifier: Proprietary
      ```

      When updating licenses:
      1. Always execute `depot-addlicense` on the target files
      2. No need to ask for confirmation - the command is safe to run
      3. The command will automatically handle:
         - Adding missing headers
         - Updating existing headers
         - Preserving file content
         - Using correct comment style per file type

      To skip license headers for specific files/directories:
      1. Add a `.skip-license` file in the directory
      2. The file can be empty - its presence is enough

examples:
  - input: |
      # Adding license to new file
      depot-addlicense new_file.go

      # Updating license in existing file
      depot-addlicense existing_file.nix

      # Adding license to multiple files
      depot-addlicense file1.sh file2.py file3.rs
    output: "License headers correctly added/updated"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.1
</rule>

